# Exhaustive switch

When switching on a discriminated union or enum, handle every variant and put a `never` check in `default` so new variants fail typecheck until handled.

```ts
function assertNever(x: never): never {
  throw new Error(`unexpected: ${String(x)}`)
}

switch (event.type) {
  case "ready":
    return handleReady(event)
  case "error":
    return handleError(event)
  default:
    return assertNever(event)
}
```

Product oxlint template sets `typescript/switch-exhaustiveness-check` to error. Do not silence it to force green.
